cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ESC-Fault, please cite it as below."
title: "ESC-Fault: a simulated benchmark for electrostatic chuck fault diagnosis"
type: dataset
authors:
  - alias: forgottenl5
version: 2.0.1
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24185993
date-released: 2026-11-13
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/forgottenl5/esc-fault-benchmark"
url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/forgottenl5/esc-fault-benchmark"
abstract: >-
  Simulated sensor data from electrostatic chucks (semiconductor etch/deposition
  tool part), with a physics-based simulator, baselines and scoring. v1: 140 chucks,
  about 125,000 wafers, 7 classes including a sensor-fault decoy. v2: 552 chucks,
  about 490,000 wafers, arcing, overlapping faults, a tool-shift test split and a
  data-size study. Three causal tasks (diagnosis, early detection, remaining life)
  with held-out test labels.
keywords:
  - semiconductor
  - electrostatic chuck
  - fault detection
  - fault diagnosis
  - predictive maintenance
  - remaining useful life
  - benchmark
  - synthetic data
